    "updated_at": "2021-05-12T16:29:43Z",
    "body": "You'd have to keep them alive for the lifetime of the object the attribute is associated with, which isn't necessarily great as it would just be a normal mutable JavaScript object not necessarily representing the actual state of things (even if the actual state of things is immutable, say, as the object could be modified by any caller).",
